WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.222
New York and

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.449
California age gating

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.168
rules go into

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:03.687
effect

00:00:04.206 --> 00:00:05.597
The EFF explains

00:00:05.409 --> 00:00:06.670
the age-verification

00:00:06.482 --> 00:00:07.531
rules New York

00:00:07.414 --> 00:00:08.722
and California are

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:09.630
putting into effect

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:09.925
in the new

00:00:09.737 --> 00:00:10.267
year

00:00:10.444 --> 00:00:11.210
and what they

00:00:11.022 --> 00:00:12.059
mean for online

00:00:11.871 --> 00:00:13.026
services and their

00:00:12.838 --> 00:00:13.569
users

00:00:14.086 --> 00:00:15.277
In California

00:00:15.383 --> 00:00:16.928
AB 1709

00:00:17.105 --> 00:00:18.897
AB 1043 and

00:00:18.744 --> 00:00:20.689
SB 976 are

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:21.350
slated to take

00:00:21.161 --> 00:00:23.048
effect on January 1

00:00:23.582 --> 00:00:24.265
First

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.459
SB 976 requires

00:00:26.271 --> 00:00:27.615
verifiable parental

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:29.065
consent before platforms

00:00:28.948 --> 00:00:30.362
can offer algorithmic

00:00:30.174 --> 00:00:31.671
feeds or nighttime

00:00:31.483 --> 00:00:33.039
notifications to anyone

00:00:32.851 --> 00:00:33.735
under 18

00:00:34.254 --> 00:00:35.268
Full story on

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:35.975
the dashboard
